<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! ~ Dispatcher

The root dispatch sigil. `<<~ name p1 p2 …>>` routes to the `\widget ~name` or
`\procedure ~name` body registered in the current tiddler scope.

The `~` widget receives `name` and `p1`–`p5` positional arguments and transcludes
`$variable=[name prefixed with ~]`. This makes every operator-defined `\widget ~sigil`
callable as `<<~ sigil args>>` without any JS registration.

The `~` dispatcher carries the SharktoothSigil tag, making it first-class in the
grammar: new sigils need only a tiddler — no code change required.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ sense the sigil name — what named body does this invocation reach?
⏿ orient: dispatcher looks up `~name` in TW5 procedure/widget namespace; delegates via $transclude
   ⚠ A SECOND WORD NAMING A CHILD SLOT OPENS A COMPOUND. `<<~ season kau …>>` resolves `~season~kau`,
     never `~season` with a positional `kau` — the child-slot words stand as `ahu` and `kau`, and any
     sigil whose second word spells one of them binds a compound head. Measured against a definition
     that stood and a call that reached nothing.
   ⚠ AND THE SPACE AFTER THE SHARKTOOTH BINDS. `<<~name …>>` written tight opens no head and falls to
     the gradient; the space carries the decision. Measured across 365 calls that each looked live.
◇ name MUST match a declared `\widget ~name` or `\procedure ~name` in accessible scope
▶ emit a TRANSCLUDE naming `~name` directly, carrying p1–p5, the argument run whole as `args`,
  the verbatim source as `src`, and every NAMED parameter the call bound — TiddlyWiki hands a
  procedure only the parameters it declares, so a generic forwarder could pass none of them on
↺ named body renders in place; no edge created; pure render-time delegation. Where the name
  resolves to nothing the transclude renders its CHILDREN — the sigil's own text — which lands on
  the gradient's floor. The `~` widget stays for INDIRECT dispatch, where a definition hands down a
  name handed down to it, and a blank name there resolves to nothing rather than to the widget itself

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Law (Kānāwai)

The dispatcher MUST route via `\widget ~` — not direct JS widget lookup.
The dispatcher MUST accept `name` and `p1`–`p5` positional arguments only.
The dispatcher MUST NOT carry `mode=` or other render-posture params — posture lives in the named body.
A dispatched sigil MUST be declared as `\widget ~name` or `\procedure ~name` in accessible tiddler scope.
Undefined names resolve to empty output (TW5 missing-variable behavior) — MUST NOT throw.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/syntax>>

!! Syntax

```text
<<~ name>>
<<~ name uri>>
<<~ name arg1 arg2>>
```

TW5 wikitext body:
```
\widget ~(name p1:"" p2:"" p3:"" p4:"" p5:"")
<$transclude $variable={{{ [<name>addprefix[~]] }}} p1=<<p1>> p2=<<p2>> p3=<<p3>> p4=<<p4>> p5=<<p5>>/>
\end
```

<<~/ahu>>

